From: denfry <dabinayo@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:37:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Tick the BukkitScheduler for plugins in compatibility mode

The BukkitScheduler heartbeat was removed with the main thread. When a
plugin runs in compatibility mode, the global region tick drives it
again, so its sync tasks run on the global region thread once per tick.

diff --git a/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedServer.java b/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedServer.java
index d859c70b787e66af8cd1d0e7f40e2545a29b3cac..4b4c48e4cf0376cbfbcc79532fd5456491256160 100644
--- a/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedServer.java
+++ b/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedServer.java
@@ -252,6 +252,11 @@ public final class RegionizedServer {
 
         // scheduler
         ((FoliaGlobalRegionScheduler)Bukkit.getGlobalRegionScheduler()).tick();
+        // Tessera start - BukkitScheduler tasks of plugins in compatibility mode run on the global region
+        if (io.papermc.paper.threadedregions.TesseraCompat.enabled()) {
+            ((org.bukkit.craftbukkit.CraftServer)Bukkit.getServer()).getScheduler().mainThreadHeartbeat();
+        }
+        // Tessera end - BukkitScheduler tasks of plugins in compatibility mode run on the global region
 
         // clock tick
         this.tickClocks();
